# SvelteKit — CursorRules Pro

You are an expert SvelteKit and Svelte 5 developer. Follow these rules strictly.

## Project Conventions
- SvelteKit with Svelte 5 runes syntax. Use TypeScript for all `.ts` and `<script lang="ts">` files.
- File naming: `+page.svelte`, `+layout.svelte`, `+server.ts` follow SvelteKit conventions. Components: PascalCase.
- Place reusable components in `$lib/components/`, utilities in `$lib/utils/`, types in `$lib/types/`.
- Use the `$lib` alias for all imports from the lib directory. Never use relative paths with `../`.
- Enable `strict: true` in tsconfig.json. No `any` types.

## Svelte 5 Runes
- Use `$state()` for reactive state. Never use the legacy `let x = value` reactive declarations.
- Use `$derived()` for computed values. Replace `$: computed = ...` with `let computed = $derived(...)`.
- Use `$effect()` for side effects. Replace `$: { ... }` blocks with `$effect(() => { ... })`.
- Use `$props()` for component props: `let { name, count = 0 }: Props = $props()`.
- Use `$bindable()` for two-way binding props when needed.

## Load Functions & Data
- Fetch data in `+page.ts` (universal) or `+page.server.ts` (server-only) load functions.
- Always type load function return values. Use `PageLoad` and `PageServerLoad` types.
- Access loaded data with `export let data: PageData` in page components.
- Use `depends()` and `invalidate()` for fine-grained cache invalidation.
- Throw `error(404)` or `redirect(303, '/login')` from load functions for control flow.

## Form Actions
- Use SvelteKit form actions for mutations — define in `+page.server.ts` with `actions`.
- Use progressive enhancement: `<form method="POST" use:enhance>`.
- Return validation errors from actions using `fail(400, { errors })`.
- Handle multiple actions per page: `?/create`, `?/delete` with named actions.
- Use `$page.form` to access action return data for inline error display.

## Stores & State
- Use Svelte 5 runes for component-local state. Use stores for cross-component shared state.
- Create stores in `$lib/stores/` — use writable, readable, and derived stores.
- For server state, prefer load functions and invalidation over client-side stores.
- Use context API (`setContext`/`getContext`) for dependency injection within component trees.
- Never mutate store values directly — use `.update()` or `.set()` methods.

## Routing & Navigation
- Use file-based routing. Group related routes with `(group)` directories.
- Use `+layout.ts` for shared data loading across route segments.
- Implement route guards in `+layout.server.ts` by checking auth and throwing `redirect`.
- Use `$page.url` and `$page.params` for accessing route information.
- Prefetch data with `data-sveltekit-preload-data="hover"` on links.

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS with `@apply` sparingly — prefer utility classes in markup.
- Scope component styles in `<style>` blocks. Use `:global()` only when necessary.
- Use CSS custom properties for theming: `var(--color-primary)`.
- Follow mobile-first responsive design with Tailwind breakpoints.

## Server-Side Rendering
- Default to SSR. Only disable for pages that genuinely cannot render on the server.
- Use `+page.server.ts` for data that requires server-only resources (DB, secrets, APIs).
- Set appropriate caching headers in load functions and API routes.
- Use streaming with `await` blocks in Svelte for deferred data loading.

## API Routes
- Define API endpoints in `+server.ts` files with `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE` exports.
- Parse and validate request bodies with Zod schemas.
- Return proper HTTP status codes and consistent JSON response shapes.
- Use hooks (`hooks.server.ts`) for global request processing: auth, logging, CORS.

## Testing
- Use Vitest for unit tests and Playwright for end-to-end tests.
- Test components with `@testing-library/svelte`. Test behavior, not implementation.
- Test load functions and form actions as standalone functions with mocked dependencies.
- Place test files adjacent to source: `Component.svelte` → `Component.test.ts`.

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Do NOT use Svelte 4 syntax (`$:`, `export let`) when Svelte 5 runes are available.
- Do NOT fetch data in `onMount` — use load functions for SSR-compatible data fetching.
- Do NOT put secrets in universal load functions (`+page.ts`) — they run in the browser.
- Do NOT use `goto()` in load functions — use `redirect()` instead.
- Do NOT create API routes for operations that form actions can handle.
- Do NOT skip `use:enhance` on forms — without it, forms cause full page reloads.
